F-0044 hook patch, written by Smith 24 Oct 2026 20:22. Not applied: a scheduled run cannot edit the hook.

Why: the E-001 edge watcher (edges/E-001/com.proteus.e001.plist, StartInterval 120 s) has been
unloaded since 22 Oct 21:19Z and D-015 is catching nothing. launchctl is off the unattended list, so
no scheduled run can reload it. This adds launchctl_ok: list/print read-only; load, unload, bootstrap,
bootout only for a plist inside the folder or a com.proteus.*.plist under ~/Library/LaunchAgents
(where the 14 Oct amendment put the graduation watcher), domain targets gui/<uid>[/com.proteus.*].
The plist decides what runs, so the fence is the plist's location, as it is for scripts.

Apply from an interactive session:
  git -C /Users/triton/PROTEUS apply --check /Users/triton/PROTEUS/state/loop/hook-patches/F-0044.diff
  git -C /Users/triton/PROTEUS apply /Users/triton/PROTEUS/state/loop/hook-patches/F-0044.diff
  python3 /Users/triton/PROTEUS/bin/test-hook.py        (12 new cases below, 6 allow, 6 deny)
then reload the watcher, which is what the finding is about:
  launchctl load /Users/triton/PROTEUS/edges/E-001/com.proteus.e001.plist
and close the finding: python3 /Users/triton/PROTEUS/bin/findings.py fix F-0044 --commit <hash> --note 'launchctl_ok in the hook; E-001 watcher reloaded'
Line numbers are against 1528571 (24 Oct); git apply tolerates offsets.

